<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<wml>

  <card id="crosstab" title="Sales Cross Analysis">

    <!--
      WapForm for Web — sales cross-analysis example (salesperson/customer x year/month)

      This version is rewritten from the carefully tuned version that is confirmed to work. Earlier versions
      used AROW/ACOL/CELL (the crosstab's internal grid indexes, 0-based); this one uses
      cellrow/cellcol/cell (counters that increase naturally while <tr>/<td> are rendered,
      1-based, backed by Wap.RowNumber/Wap.ColNumber, not specific to crosstab).
      They are two completely different sets of variables, not a case difference — cell matches CELL because
      SetVar/GetVar both UpperCase(Name) before looking up, so identifiers are
      case-insensitive; but cellrow/cellcol and AROW/ACOL are two independent sets of variables, and that was
      the real cause of the earlier crosstab crashes, not the or keyword (that was a
      misdiagnosis; compound conditions such as (cellrow<3) or (cellcol<3) are used as is here,
      with no need to rewrite them as elseif).

      The SQL sums the amounts with group by first, so each (month, salesperson, customer) has only
      one row; the crosstab's Cell() accumulation then only handles "the first write to this cell",
      without relying on it to accumulate duplicates, which is more predictable.

      With data spanning two years, the two column groupings yy (outer column, year) →
      ym (inner column, year-month) are correct across years; with a single year
      the outer yy grouping always has one value, and the year boundary could not be tested.

      rows="20" cols="15" control paging (Wap.LinesPerPage/CrossRow/CrossCol):
      when the data has more rows/columns than this, the output pages automatically.

      [Fixed] The dialog= attribute is only parsed, not used, by the current engine (Dlg is a local variable
      that is only assigned and never read anywhere in the source), so writing it has no effect.

      But autospan="yes" really does work — it was earlier mistaken for dead code like dialog=;
      reading the source of _td showed that AutoSpan is a TCard field that _crosstab only sets,
      and _td is what actually uses it — two separate pieces of logic. It works as a standard two-pass "measure, then merge":
      Printable=0 (measure pass) compares adjacent cells, and when they are the same, adds the count of
      identical consecutive cells to ColArray/RowArray; Printable=1 (render pass) reads that count back,
      and when it is greater than 1 outputs colspan=/rowspan= to merge those cells into one. This applies only to
      the header area (the salesperson/customer/year/month columns and rows); data cells are not affected. That is why
      the salesperson code "10" appears only once, vertically centered — it is not a CSS illusion;
      the browser really receives a rowspan cell, and centering the content is the browser's default for
      rowspan cells.
    -->

    <div class="narrow">
      <div class="wf-head">
        <div class="wf-badge">WapForm for Web · Example</div>
        <div class="wf-title">Sales Cross Analysis</div>
        <div class="wf-sub">2026/01 ~ 2026/09, cross-tabulated by salesperson/customer (rows) and year/month (columns).</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <dbquery id="xy">
      <![CDATA[
select
  year(s.sdate)                          yy,
  date_format(s.sdate, '%Y%m')           ym,
  s.Eno                                  eno,
  s.Cno                                  cno,
  sum(coalesce(s.Amount, 0))             amount
from sh s
left join cu c on c.Cno = s.Cno
where s.sdate >= '2026-01-01' and s.sdate < '2026-10-01'
group by 
  date_format(s.sdate, '%Y%m'),
  s.Eno,
  s.Cno
order by yy, ym, eno, cno
    ]]>
    </dbquery>
    <div class="xtab-wrap">
    <crosstab dataset="xy" dialog="cno;sdate" field="amount" autospan="yes">
      <setvar name="I" value="0"/>
      <setvar name="J" value="0"/>
      <setvar name="K" value="0"/>
      <setvar name="N" value="0"/>
      <setvar name="T" value="0"/>
      <setvar name="C" value="''"/>
      <setvar name="R" value="''"/>
      <setvar name="A" value="0"/>
      <setvar name="B" value="0"/>
      <setvar name="X" value="[1..999]"/>
      <setvar name="Y" value="[1..999]"/>
      <page>
        <table class="xtab-table" rows="20" cols="15">
          <row change="xy.eno">
            <setvar name="I" value="1"/>
            <while cnd="I&lt;=99">
              <setvar name="X[I]" value="0"/>
              <setvar name="I" value="I+1"/>
            </while>
            <row change="xy.cno">
              <setvar name="K" value="0"/>
              <setvar name="B" value="0"/>
              <tr>
                <col change="xy.YY">
                  <setvar name="A" value="0"/>
                  <col change="xy.YM">
                    <log message="$cellrow $cellcol $cell"/>
                    <setvar name="C" value="cell"/>
                    <setvar name="R" value="cell" cnd="cellcol=1"/>
                    <setvar name="N" value="0"/>
                    <if cnd="(cellrow&lt;3) or (cellcol&lt;3)">
                      <if cnd="(cellrow=2) and (cellcol&lt;3)">
                      <td width="120" align="center"><i>$(IF(cell='',' ',cell))</i></td>
                      <else/>
                      <td align="center">$(IF(cell='',' ',cell))</td>
                      </if>
                      <else/>
                      <setvar name="N" value="VAL(cell)"/>
                      <td width="60" align="right">$(IF(N=0,' ',FORMAT('%d',N)))</td>
                      <setvar name="A" value="A+N"/>
                      <setvar name="B" value="B+N"/>
                      <setvar name="K" value="K+1"/>
                      <setvar name="X[K]" value="X[K]+N"/>
                      <setvar name="Y[K]" value="Y[K]+N"/>
                    </if>
                  </col>
                  <if cnd="cellcol&gt;3">
                    <if cnd="cellrow=1">
                      <th width="60" align="center">$C</th>
                    </if>
                    <if cnd="cellrow=2">
                      <th width="60" align="center">TOTAL</th>
                    </if>
                    <if cnd="cellrow&gt;2">
                      <td align="right">$(FORMAT('%d',A))</td>
                    </if>
                    <setvar name="K" value="K+1"/>
                    <setvar name="X[K]" value="X[K]+A"/>
                    <setvar name="Y[K]" value="Y[K]+A"/>
                  </if>
                </col>
                <if cnd="cellrow=1">
                  <th width="60" align="center"> </th>
                </if>
                <if cnd="cellrow=2">
                  <th width="60" align="center">AMOUNT</th>
                </if>
                <if cnd="cellrow&gt;2">
                  <td align="right">$(FORMAT('%d',B))</td>
                </if>
                <setvar name="K" value="K+1"/>
                <setvar name="X[K]" value="X[K]+B"/>
                <setvar name="Y[K]" value="Y[K]+B"/>
              </tr>
            </row>
            <if cnd="cellrow&gt;3">
              <tr class="xtab-total-row">
                <th width="60">$R</th>
                <th width="60">TOTAL</th>
                <setvar name="I" value="1"/>
                <while cnd="I&lt;=K">
                  <td width="60" align="right">$(FORMAT('%d',X[I]))</td>
                  <setvar name="I" value="I+1"/>
                </while>
              </tr>
            </if>
          </row>
          <tr class="xtab-grand-row">
            <th width="60"> </th>
            <th width="60">AMOUNT</th>
            <setvar name="I" value="1"/>
            <while cnd="I&lt;=K">
              <td width="60" align="right">$(FORMAT('%d',Y[I]))</td>
              <setvar name="I" value="I+1"/>
            </while>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </page>
    </crosstab>
    </div>

    <div class="narrow">
      <div class="foot">
        Layout comes from <code>wapform.htm</code>; the data and cross-tab logic are defined in <code>crosstab.wml</code>.<br/>
        Data source <code>sh</code> (sales order headers), period 2026/01 ~ 2026/09; amounts are summed in SQL with
        <code>group by</code> first, so the cross table only has to place each value in its cell.<br/>
        It uses the same data as the <a href="report.wml">grouped report</a>, presented differently — one is
        a row x column cross matrix, the other a grouped list report.<br/>
        More examples: <a href="multiupload.wml">File Upload</a>, <a href="chart.wml">Chart Components</a>,
        <a href="report.wml">Grouped Sales Report</a>, <a href="linepush.wml?push_userid=&amp;push_text=">LINE Push</a>, <a href="function.wml">Function Self-Test</a>.
      </div>
    </div>

  </card>

</wml>
